\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.2}{\ignorespaces Initial-condition hand-off. From each CosmoGridV1 run's stored linear perturbations, the CDM+baryon transfer function at $a=1$ is extracted in \textsc  {class} table format (\texttt  {pkdgrav/get\_transfer\_function.py}); a matched \textsc  {class} solve with three massive neutrino states supplies the derived $\sigma _8$ and $\Omega _r$; \texttt  {IC\_preparation.py} patches these into \texttt  {cosmology.par}; \textsc  {PkdGrav3} generates the backscaled particle load, which both solvers then consume byte-identically.}}{15}{}\protected@file@percent }
