\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.3}{\ignorespaces Streaming shell accumulation. The integration grid is the sorted union of all shell edges, so each sub-step sweeps exactly one radial shell (highlighted). Per step, only the pre- and post-step particle states are alive; their lightcone crossings (Sec.~\ref {sec:crossing}) are pixelised and added to that shell's running count map, after which the pre-step state is discarded. Memory usage is thus $\mathcal  {O}(1)$ snapshots $+\tmspace  +\thickmuskip {.2777em}S$ maps, independent of the number of steps.}}{17}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:shell_stream}{{2.3}{17}{}{figure.2.3}{}}
