\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{Preconditioned denoiser.}{23}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{eq:edm_precond}{{2.21}{23}{}{equation.2.21}{}}
\abx@aux@cite{0}{karras_elucidating_2022}
\abx@aux@segm{0}{0}{karras_elucidating_2022}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.8}{\ignorespaces Scalar conditioning in the shared U-Net (\texttt  {FlowUNet} / \texttt  {DenoiserUNet}). (a) The single scalar -- the flow time $t$ or the noise embedding $c_{\mathrm  {noise}}(\sigma )$ -- is lifted onto 64 sinusoids of geometrically spaced frequencies (plus their cosines) and expanded by a two-layer MLP into a 512-dimensional embedding: low frequencies encode coarse position along the trajectory, high frequencies fine position. (b) Inside every double-convolution block, a block-specific linear layer projects this shared embedding to one $(\gamma _c, \beta _c)$ pair per channel, applied as a feature-wise affine transform between the two convolutions -- FiLM changes what the channels \emph  {contain}, never how many there are. (c) The same embedding modulates every encoder, bottleneck, and decoder block, so one network represents the full trajectory-dependent map; the cosmology--redshift vector instead enters once, additively and zero-initialised, at the bottleneck.}}{24}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:film_unet}{{2.8}{24}{}{figure.2.8}{}}
\newlabel{eq:edm_coeffs}{{2.22}{24}{}{equation.2.22}{}}
\abx@aux@cite{0}{karras_elucidating_2022}
\abx@aux@segm{0}{0}{karras_elucidating_2022}
\abx@aux@cite{0}{karras_elucidating_2022}
\abx@aux@segm{0}{0}{karras_elucidating_2022}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{Training.}{25}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{eq:edm_loss}{{2.23}{25}{}{equation.2.23}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{Sampling.}{25}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{eq:karras_schedule}{{2.24}{25}{}{equation.2.24}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.9}{\ignorespaces The diffusion pipeline (\texttt  {ml/diffusion/model.py}). Top: the EDM denoiser is the U-Net of Figure~\ref {fig:film_unet} wrapped in the four preconditioning coefficients of Eq.~\eqref  {eq:edm_coeffs} -- the input is variance-normalised by $c_{\mathrm  {in}}$ and concatenated with the (never-noised) low patch; the output blends an identity path ($c_{\mathrm  {skip}}\,x_t$) with the network's contribution ($c_{\mathrm  {out}} F_\theta $), shifting smoothly from ``pass through'' at low $\sigma $ to ``generate'' at high $\sigma $; $c_{\mathrm  {noise}}$ feeds $\sigma $ to the FiLM conditioning. Bottom: sampling starts from pure noise and applies 32 Heun steps down the Karras schedule, each invoking $D_\theta $ up to twice; the final sample is the high-pass residual, composed onto the low map so the large scales remain Disco-DJ's exactly.}}{26}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:edm_sampling}{{2.9}{26}{}{figure.2.9}{}}
