\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces The 198 runnable grid cosmologies (gray) and the 30 held-out validation cosmologies (blue) in the sampled $w$CDM parameter space (\texttt  {ml/analysis/plot\_cosmo\_params.py}). The held-out set spans the full ranges of $\Omega _m$, $\sigma _8$, $w_0$, $H_0$, $n_s$, and $\Omega _b$, so the reported performance probes genuine interpolation across the grid, not proximity to training cosmologies.}}{30}{}\protected@file@percent }
